##chal27
vaca= ["Japan", "China", "Mexico", "Fiji", "Thailand", "Italy"]
print("This is your list of destinations: Japan, China, Mexico, Fiji, Thailand, Italy \n1.Add a travel destination \n2.Find a travel destination \n3. Remove a travel destination \n4. Sort destinations by alphabet \n5. Count destinations: ")
choice=int(input())

if (choice==1):
    newdest= input("What destination would you like to add:")
    vaca.append(newdest)
    print(vaca)
elif (choice==2):
    finddest= input("Which travel destination would you like to find: ")
    if finddest in vaca:
        print(vaca)
    else:
        print("Not in list")
elif (choice==3):
    removeitem= input("which item would you like to remove: ")
    vaca.remove(removeitem)
    print(vaca)
elif (choice==4):
    vaca.sort()
    print(vaca)
else:
    print("invalid")

    Write a program that checks if the input string has an “e", and if it does, print "Has e". Otherwise, print “invalid input”. Remember you can use string functions that you learned before to help you.

gro=["apple", "yogurt", "milk", "rice", "avacados", "chicken"]
print("You can \n1. add an item\n2. Print list\n3. Sort items\n4. Remove an item\n5. count groceries\n6. replace grocery item")
choice=int(input())

if (choice==1):
    additem= input("What item would you like to add?: ")
    gro.append(additem)
    print(gro)
elif (choice==2):
    print(gro)
elif (choice==3):
    gro.sort()
    print(gro)
elif (choice==4):
    removeitem = input("What item would you like to remove?:")
    gro.remove(removeitem)
    print(gro)
elif (choice==5):
    gro.count(gro)
    print(gro)
else:
    print("invalid")


